/-!
# The table row `E₆⁴` is the ternary tetracode gluing of `(E₆)⁴`

The twelfth row of Conway--Sloane's Table 16.1, `TauCeti.RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth`, glues four
orthogonal copies of the `E₆` root lattice along the subgroup `e6Fourth.glueSubgroup` generated by
the cyclic pattern `[1(012)]`, whose expanded words `[1012]`, `[1120]`, `[1201]` satisfy
`[1012] + [1120] + [1201] = 0` in `(ℤ/3)⁴` and span a subgroup of order `9`.

Transposing the first two `E₆` components (`Equiv.swap 0 1`) sends these three words to
`(0, 1, 1, 2)`, `(1, 1, 2, 0)`, and `(2, 1, 0, 1)`, which span the ternary tetracode
`TauCeti.tetracode` generated by `(1, 0, 1, 1)` and `(0, 1, 1, -1)`.  This file establishes that
identification at both the glue-word and lattice levels, exhibits explicit norm-`4` minuscule-weight
generators and a nine-coset simple-root coordinate criterion for `TauCeti.niemeierE6Fourth`, and
transports all monomial automorphisms of `tetracode` to self-isometries of the table lattice:

* Every nonzero `E₆` glue label has coset minimum `4/3`, so the shortest norm `μ(w)` of an `E₆`
  glue word is `4/3` times its Hamming weight
  (`TauCeti.DynkinType.sum_glueMinimum_E6_eq_four_div_three_mul_hammingNorm`).
* Under the coordinate swap `e6FourthTetracodePerm = Equiv.swap 0 1`, the glue-word isometry
  `e6FourthTetracodeIsometry` carries `e6Fourth.glueSubgroup` onto `tetracode`
  (`map_glueSubgroup_e6FourthTetracodeIsometry`).  In the unpermuted table coordinates
  `(u₀, u₁, u₂, u₃) ∈ (ℤ/3)⁴`, membership in `e6Fourth.glueSubgroup` is cut out by the linear
  equations `u₂ = u₀ + u₁` and `u₃ = u₁ - u₀` (`mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_iff`).  Because every
  nonzero tetracode word has Hamming weight `3`, every nonzero glue word of `e6Fourth` has exact
  shortest norm `4` (`sum_glueMinimum_eq_four_of_mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_of_ne_zero`).
* Lifting `e6FourthTetracodePerm` to the orthogonal sum of root lattices produces the explicit
  isometry `niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry` from `niemeierE6Fourth` onto the overlattice of
  `typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower (Fin 4)` glued along `tetracode`.
* Realizing the two `𝔽₃`-basis glue words `[0111]` and `[1012]` by `(0, ϖ₁, ϖ₁, ϖ₁)` and
  `(ϖ₁, 0, ϖ₁, -ϖ₁)` using `typeE₆MinusculeWeight` gives two norm-`4` vectors
  `e6FourthGlueVector 0` and `e6FourthGlueVector 1` that generate `niemeierE6Fourth` over
  `e6Fourth.rootLattice` (`niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_eq_sup_span`) and yield an explicit nine-coset
  integrality criterion in Bourbaki simple-root coordinates
  (`mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_iff_int_coords`).
* Any monomial automorphism `signedEquiv v e ∈ monomialAut C` of an isotropic ternary code `C` acts
  by a self-isometry `typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry` on the corresponding `(E₆)^ι` overlattice;
  conjugating across `niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry` transports `monomialAut tetracode` to
  self-isometries `niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry` of `niemeierE6Fourth`.

The comparison and automorphism-transport pattern follows
`TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.IntegralLattice.Rank24.A2Twelfth` and
`TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.IntegralLattice.Rank24.TableRow.A2Twelfth` by the Tau Ceti contributors.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.sum_glueMinimum_E6_eq_four_div_three_mul_hammingNorm`: over `E₆`, the coset
  minimum of a glue word is `4/3` times its Hamming weight.
* `TauCeti.RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry`,
  `TauCeti.RootfulNiemeierType.map_glueSubgroup_e6FourthTetracodeIsometry`,
  `TauCeti.RootfulNiemeierType.mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_iff`: identification of
  `e6Fourth.glueSubgroup` with `TauCeti.tetracode` and its explicit linear equations.
* `TauCeti.RootfulNiemeierType.sum_glueMinimum_eq_four_of_mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_of_ne_zero`,
  `TauCeti.RootfulNiemeierType.image_vectorsOfNorm_niemeierE6Fourth_eq`: exact shortest norm `4` of
  all nonzero glue words and agreement of low-norm shells (`< 4`) with `e6Fourth.rootLattice`.
* `TauCeti.niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry`: the isometry from `niemeierE6Fourth` onto the
  ternary tetracode gluing of `(E₆)⁴`.
* `TauCeti.e6FourthGlueVector`, `TauCeti.form_e6FourthGlueVector_self`,
  `TauCeti.niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_eq_sup_span`,
  `TauCeti.mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_iff_exists_fin_three`,
  `TauCeti.mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_iff_int_coords`: explicit norm-`4` minuscule-weight
  generators and nine-coset carrier criteria for `niemeierE6Fourth`.
* `TauCeti.typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry`,
  `TauCeti.niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry`: lattice self-isometries induced by monomial
  automorphisms of isotropic ternary codes and of `tetracode`.

## References

* J. H. Conway and N. J. A. Sloane, *Sphere Packings, Lattices and Groups*, 3rd ed., Chapter 4,
  §§3 and 8.3, and Chapter 16, §1, Table 16.1.
* W. Ebeling, *Lattices and Codes*, 3rd ed., §3.3.
-/

public section

open Matrix

namespace TauCeti

namespace DynkinType

/-- **The shortest norm of an `E₆` glue word is four thirds of its Hamming weight**: each nonzero
label of the `E₆` alphabet `ℤ/3` has shortest norm `4/3`. -/
theorem sum_glueMinimum_E6_eq_four_div_three_mul_hammingNorm {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]
    (ht : E6.IsSimplyLaced) (w : ι → ZMod 3) :
    ∑ i, E6.glueMinimum ht (w i) = 4 / 3 * hammingNorm w := by
  simp only [glueMinimum_E6, hammingNorm, Finset.sum_ite, Finset.sum_const_zero, Finset.sum_const,
    nsmul_eq_mul, zero_add, mul_comm]

end DynkinType

open DynkinType FiniteQuadraticModule IntegralLattice

namespace RootfulNiemeierType

/-! ### Components and tetracode identification of the glue subgroup -/

/-- The row `E₆⁴` has four components. -/
@[simp]
theorem length_components_e6Fourth : e6Fourth.components.length = 4 :=
  List.length_replicate

/-- Every component of the row `E₆⁴` has type `E₆`. -/
@[simp]
theorem componentType_e6Fourth (i : Fin e6Fourth.components.length) :
    e6Fourth.componentType i = E6 :=
  congrArg Subtype.val (List.getElem_replicate _)

/-- The glue words of the row `E₆⁴` read directly as ternary words in four copies of the standard
`E₆` glue alphabet `ℤ/3`, keeping the order of the table components. -/
noncomputable abbrev e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry :
    FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry e6Fourth.glueModule
      (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) :=
  e6Fourth.glueModuleIsometry (fun _ ↦ isSimplyLaced_E6) rfl
    fun i ↦ (componentType_e6Fourth i).symm

/-- **The coordinate transposition of the `E₆⁴` comparison**: swapping the first two `E₆`
components carries the Conway--Sloane cyclic pattern `[1(012)]` onto the ternary tetracode. -/
@[expose] def e6FourthTetracodePerm : Equiv.Perm (Fin 4) :=
  Equiv.swap 0 1

/-- `e6FourthTetracodePerm` is the transposition of `0` and `1` in `Fin 4`. -/
theorem e6FourthTetracodePerm_def : e6FourthTetracodePerm = Equiv.swap 0 1 :=
  (rfl)

/-- `e6FourthTetracodePerm` is involutive, so its inverse is itself. -/
@[simp]
theorem symm_e6FourthTetracodePerm : e6FourthTetracodePerm.symm = e6FourthTetracodePerm :=
  Equiv.symm_swap 0 1

/-- **The `E₆⁴` glue words in tetracode coordinates**: reading the four components as copies of
`ℤ/3` and swapping the first two coordinates gives a quadratic-module isometry into the standard
four-coordinate `E₆` alphabet. -/
noncomputable def e6FourthTetracodeIsometry :
    FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry e6Fourth.glueModule
      (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) :=
  e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry.trans
    (FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.coordinatePowerSigned typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule 1
      e6FourthTetracodePerm)

/-- At tetracode coordinate `j : Fin 4`, `e6FourthTetracodeIsometry` reads the unpermuted table
label at `e6FourthTetracodePerm j`. -/
@[simp]
theorem e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply (w : e6Fourth.glueModule) (j : Fin 4) :
    (e6FourthTetracodeIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) j =
      (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) (e6FourthTetracodePerm j) := by
  have h := FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.coordinatePowerSigned_apply
    typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule 1 e6FourthTetracodePerm (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w) j
  rw [symm_e6FourthTetracodePerm, Pi.one_apply, one_smul] at h
  exact h

private theorem glueWords_e6Fourth :
    e6Fourth.glueWords = {[1, 0, 1, 2], [1, 1, 2, 0], [1, 2, 0, 1]} := by
  decide

private def e6DigitsWord (d : Fin 4 → Fin 3) : Fin 4 → E6.glueAlphabet isSimplyLaced_E6 :=
  fun j ↦ ((d j : ℕ) : ZMod 3)

private theorem decodeGlueWord_E6_four_ofFn (d : Fin 4 → Fin 3) :
    decodeGlueWord (fun _ : Fin 4 ↦ E6) (fun _ ↦ isSimplyLaced_E6)
        (List.ofFn fun j ↦ ((d j : Fin 3) : ℕ)) =
      some (e6DigitsWord d) := by
  rw [decodeGlueWord_ofFn _ _ _ fun j ↦ (d j).isLt]
  congr 1
  funext j
  exact glueLabelEquiv_E6 isSimplyLaced_E6 (d j)

private theorem decoded_glueWords_e6Fourth :
    {w : Fin 4 → E6.glueAlphabet isSimplyLaced_E6 |
        ∃ l ∈ e6Fourth.glueWords,
          decodeGlueWord (fun _ : Fin 4 ↦ E6) (fun _ ↦ isSimplyLaced_E6) l = some w} =
      {e6DigitsWord ![1, 0, 1, 2], e6DigitsWord ![1, 1, 2, 0], e6DigitsWord ![1, 2, 0, 1]} := by
  have h0 : ([1, 0, 1, 2] : List ℕ) = List.ofFn fun j : Fin 4 ↦ ((![1, 0, 1, 2] j : Fin 3) : ℕ) :=
    rfl
  have h1 : ([1, 1, 2, 0] : List ℕ) = List.ofFn fun j : Fin 4 ↦ ((![1, 1, 2, 0] j : Fin 3) : ℕ) :=
    rfl
  have h2 : ([1, 2, 0, 1] : List ℕ) = List.ofFn fun j : Fin 4 ↦ ((![1, 2, 0, 1] j : Fin 3) : ℕ) :=
    rfl
  ext w
  rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, glueWords_e6Fourth]
  simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton, exists_eq_or_imp, exists_eq_left,
    h0, h1, h2, decodeGlueWord_E6_four_ofFn, Option.some.injEq, Set.mem_insert_iff,
    Set.mem_singleton_iff]
  simp only [eq_comm]

private theorem coordinatePowerSigned_e6FourthTetracodePerm_e6DigitsWord (d : Fin 4 → Fin 3) :
    (FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.coordinatePowerSigned typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule 1
        e6FourthTetracodePerm).toAddEquiv (e6DigitsWord d) =
      ((fun j : Fin 4 ↦ ((d (e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ℕ) : ZMod 3)) :
        typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) := by
  let u : typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4) := e6DigitsWord d
  funext j
  have hj := FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.coordinatePowerSigned_apply
    typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule 1 e6FourthTetracodePerm u j
  rw [symm_e6FourthTetracodePerm, Pi.one_apply, one_smul] at hj
  exact hj

/-- Each basis row `tetracodeGenerator b` (`[0111]` and `[1012]`) lies in the additive subgroup
generated by the `e6FourthTetracodePerm`-permuted table glue words `[1012]`, `[1120]`, `[1201]`. -/
private theorem tetracodeGenerator_mem_closure_e6FourthDigits (b : Fin 2) :
    (tetracodeGenerator b : typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) ∈
      AddSubgroup.closure
        (((FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.coordinatePowerSigned typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule 1
            e6FourthTetracodePerm).toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom :
              typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4) →+
                typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) ''
          ({e6DigitsWord ![1, 0, 1, 2], e6DigitsWord ![1, 1, 2, 0],
            e6DigitsWord ![1, 2, 0, 1]} :
            Set (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)))) := by
  let σ := FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.coordinatePowerSigned typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule 1
    e6FourthTetracodePerm
  set H := AddSubgroup.closure
    ((σ.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom : typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4) →+
        typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) ''
      ({e6DigitsWord ![1, 0, 1, 2], e6DigitsWord ![1, 1, 2, 0],
        e6DigitsWord ![1, 2, 0, 1]} :
        Set (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4))))
  let d1012 : Fin 4 → Fin 3 := ![1, 0, 1, 2]
  let d1120 : Fin 4 → Fin 3 := ![1, 1, 2, 0]
  fin_cases b
  · have hmem : σ.toAddEquiv (e6DigitsWord d1120) - σ.toAddEquiv (e6DigitsWord d1012) ∈ H :=
      H.sub_mem
        (AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨e6DigitsWord d1120, Or.inr (Or.inl rfl), rfl⟩)
        (AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨e6DigitsWord d1012, Or.inl rfl, rfl⟩)
    rw [coordinatePowerSigned_e6FourthTetracodePerm_e6DigitsWord,
      coordinatePowerSigned_e6FourthTetracodePerm_e6DigitsWord] at hmem
    have heq :
        ((fun j : Fin 4 ↦ ((d1120 (e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ℕ) : ZMod 3)) :
          typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) -
        ((fun j : Fin 4 ↦ ((d1012 (e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ℕ) : ZMod 3)) :
          typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) =
        (tetracodeGenerator 0 : typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) := by
      funext j
      -- Both sides evaluate in the underlying alphabet `ZMod 3`.
      change ((d1120 (e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ℕ) : ZMod 3) -
        ((d1012 (e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ℕ) : ZMod 3) = tetracodeGenerator 0 j
      rw [tetracodeGenerator_def]
      fin_cases j <;> decide
    exact Eq.mp (congrArg (· ∈ H) heq) hmem
  · have hmem : σ.toAddEquiv (e6DigitsWord d1012) ∈ H :=
      AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨e6DigitsWord d1012, Or.inl rfl, rfl⟩
    rw [coordinatePowerSigned_e6FourthTetracodePerm_e6DigitsWord] at hmem
    have heq :
        ((fun j : Fin 4 ↦ ((d1012 (e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ℕ) : ZMod 3)) :
          typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) =
        (tetracodeGenerator 1 : typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) := by
      funext j
      rw [tetracodeGenerator_def]
      fin_cases j <;> decide
    exact Eq.mp (congrArg (· ∈ H) heq) hmem

/-- **The table glue subgroup of `E₆⁴` is the ternary tetracode**: `e6FourthTetracodeIsometry`
carries the subgroup generated by `[1(012)]` onto `TauCeti.tetracode`. -/
theorem map_glueSubgroup_e6FourthTetracodeIsometry :
    (e6Fourth.glueSubgroup.map e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.toAddEquiv :
        AddSubgroup (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4))) =
      tetracode.toAddSubgroup := by
  let σ := FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.coordinatePowerSigned typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule 1
    e6FourthTetracodePerm
  let φ : e6Fourth.glueModule →+ typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4) :=
    e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom
  have hcomp : e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom =
      σ.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom.comp φ :=
    AddMonoidHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl
  have htrans : (e6Fourth.glueSubgroup.map e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.toAddEquiv :
        AddSubgroup (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4))) =
      (e6Fourth.glueSubgroup.map φ).map σ.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom :=
    (congrArg e6Fourth.glueSubgroup.map hcomp).trans (AddSubgroup.map_map _ _ _).symm
  have hsub : e6Fourth.glueSubgroup.map φ =
      AddSubgroup.closure ({e6DigitsWord ![1, 0, 1, 2], e6DigitsWord ![1, 1, 2, 0],
        e6DigitsWord ![1, 2, 0, 1]} :
          Set (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4))) :=
    (map_glueSubgroup_glueModuleIsometry e6Fourth (fun _ ↦ isSimplyLaced_E6) rfl
      fun i ↦ (componentType_e6Fourth i).symm).trans
      (congrArg AddSubgroup.closure decoded_glueWords_e6Fourth)
  rw [htrans, hsub, AddMonoidHom.map_closure]
  refine le_antisymm ((AddSubgroup.closure_le _).mpr ?_) fun x hx ↦ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨u, rfl | rfl | rfl, rfl⟩ <;>
    · rw [AddEquiv.coe_toAddMonoidHom,
        coordinatePowerSigned_e6FourthTetracodePerm_e6DigitsWord]
      exact (mem_tetracode_iff _).mpr (by decide)
  · set H := AddSubgroup.closure
      ((σ.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom : typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4) →+
          typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) ''
        ({e6DigitsWord ![1, 0, 1, 2], e6DigitsWord ![1, 1, 2, 0],
          e6DigitsWord ![1, 2, 0, 1]} :
          Set (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4))))
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := (tetracode_def ▸ Matrix.mem_generatedBy_iff).mp hx
    rw [Matrix.vecMul_eq_sum, Fin.sum_univ_two]
    have hsmul (b : Fin 2) :
        (a b • tetracodeGenerator b :
          typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) ∈ H := by
      rw [← ZMod.natCast_zmod_val (a b), Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul]
      exact H.nsmul_mem (tetracodeGenerator_mem_closure_e6FourthDigits b) _
    exact H.add_mem (hsmul 0) (hsmul 1)

/-- **Membership in the `E₆⁴` glue subgroup via the tetracode**: a glue word of the row lies in
`e6Fourth.glueSubgroup` if and only if its image under `e6FourthTetracodeIsometry` belongs to
`TauCeti.tetracode`. -/
theorem mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_iff_tetracode (w : e6Fourth.glueModule) :
    w ∈ e6Fourth.glueSubgroup ↔ (e6FourthTetracodeIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) ∈ tetracode :=
  (AddSubgroup.mem_map_iff_mem e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.toAddEquiv.injective).symm.trans
    (iff_of_eq (congrArg (e6FourthTetracodeIsometry w ∈ ·)
      map_glueSubgroup_e6FourthTetracodeIsometry))

/-- **Explicit linear equations for the `E₆⁴` glue subgroup in table coordinates**: writing
`u = (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3)`, `w` lies in `e6Fourth.glueSubgroup` if and
only if `u 2 = u 0 + u 1` and `u 3 = u 1 - u 0`. -/
theorem mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_iff (w : e6Fourth.glueModule) :
    w ∈ e6Fourth.glueSubgroup ↔
      (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) 2 =
          (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) 0 +
            (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) 1 ∧
        (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) 3 =
          (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) 1 -
            (e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) 0 := by
  let u : Fin 4 → ZMod 3 := e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w
  let v : Fin 4 → ZMod 3 := e6FourthTetracodeIsometry w
  have hv (j : Fin 4) : v j = u (e6FourthTetracodePerm j) :=
    e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply w j
  have hp : (v 2 = v 0 + v 1 ∧ v 3 = v 0 - v 1) ↔ (u 2 = u 0 + u 1 ∧ u 3 = u 1 - u 0) := by
    have p0 : e6FourthTetracodePerm 0 = 1 := rfl
    have p1 : e6FourthTetracodePerm 1 = 0 := rfl
    have p2 : e6FourthTetracodePerm 2 = 2 := rfl
    have p3 : e6FourthTetracodePerm 3 = 3 := rfl
    rw [hv 2, hv 0, hv 1, hv 3, p0, p1, p2, p3, add_comm (u 1)]
  exact (mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_iff_tetracode w).trans ((mem_tetracode_iff v).trans hp)

/-- **Every nonzero glue word of `E₆⁴` has exact shortest norm `4`**: its tetracode image has
Hamming weight `3`, and each of the three nonzero `E₆` labels contributes `4/3`. -/
theorem sum_glueMinimum_eq_four_of_mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_of_ne_zero
    {w : e6Fourth.glueModule} (hw : w ∈ e6Fourth.glueSubgroup) (hw0 : w ≠ 0) :
    ∑ i, (e6Fourth.componentType i).glueMinimum (e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType i) (w i) =
      4 := by
  let x : Fin 4 → ZMod 3 := e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w
  let y : Fin 4 → ZMod 3 := e6FourthTetracodeIsometry w
  have hmem : y ∈ tetracode := (mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_iff_tetracode w).mp hw
  have hne : y ≠ 0 :=
    (map_ne_zero_iff e6FourthTetracodeIsometry e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.injective).mpr hw0
  have hy : y = signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) 1 e6FourthTetracodePerm x := by
    funext j
    rw [signedEquiv_apply, symm_e6FourthTetracodePerm, Pi.one_apply, Units.val_one, Int.cast_one,
      one_mul]
    exact e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply w j
  have hwt : hammingNorm x = 3 := by
    rw [← hammingNorm_signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) 1 e6FourthTetracodePerm x, ← hy]
    exact hammingNorm_eq_three_of_mem_tetracode_of_ne_zero hmem hne
  have hmin : ∑ i, E6.glueMinimum isSimplyLaced_E6 (x i) = 4 / 3 * hammingNorm x :=
    sum_glueMinimum_E6_eq_four_div_three_mul_hammingNorm isSimplyLaced_E6 x
  rw [← sum_glueMinimum_glueModuleIsometry e6Fourth (fun _ ↦ isSimplyLaced_E6) rfl
      (fun i ↦ (componentType_e6Fourth i).symm) w]
  exact hmin.trans (by rw [hwt]; norm_num)

/-- **Gluing along the `E₆⁴` table subgroup adds no vectors of norm strictly below `4`**, compared
in the common ambient space. -/
theorem image_vectorsOfNorm_niemeierE6Fourth_eq {m : ℚ} (hm : m < 4) :
    (fun x : niemeierE6Fourth ↦ (x : ∀ i, Fin (e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ)) ''
        niemeierE6Fourth.vectorsOfNorm m =
      (fun x : e6Fourth.rootLattice ↦ (x : ∀ i, Fin (e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ)) ''
        e6Fourth.rootLattice.vectorsOfNorm m := by
  rw [niemeierE6Fourth, lattice_def]
  exact DynkinType.image_vectorsOfNorm_gluedLattice_eq _ _ e6Fourth.valid_componentType _ _
    (fun _ hw hw0 ↦
      (sum_glueMinimum_eq_four_of_mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_of_ne_zero hw hw0).symm.le) hm

end RootfulNiemeierType

/-! ### Comparison with the ternary tetracode gluing of `(E₆)⁴` -/

private theorem isNondegenerate_rootLattice_E6_fin6 :
    @IsNondegenerate (Fin 6 → ℚ) _ (Pi.Function.module _ _ _)
      (E6.rootLattice isSimplyLaced_E6) :=
  inferInstanceAs (E6.rootLattice isSimplyLaced_E6).IsNondegenerate

attribute [local instance] isNondegenerate_rootLattice_E6_fin6

/-- **Carrier of `niemeierE6Fourth` in tetracode coordinates**: an ambient vector lies in
`niemeierE6Fourth` if and only if it lies in the dual of `e6Fourth.rootLattice` and the glue word
of its discriminant class maps into `TauCeti.tetracode` under `e6FourthTetracodeIsometry`. -/
theorem mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_iff_tetracode
    (x : ∀ i, Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ) :
    x ∈ niemeierE6Fourth.carrier ↔
      ∃ hx : x ∈ RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice.dualCarrier,
        (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry
          ((DynkinType.glueWordIsometry RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType
              RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType
              RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType).toAddEquiv.symm
            (Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨x, hx⟩)) : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) ∈ tetracode :=
  (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.mem_lattice_carrier_iff x).trans
    (exists_congr fun _ ↦ RootfulNiemeierType.mem_glueSubgroup_e6Fourth_iff_tetracode _)

/-- Identification of the `i`-th `E₆` root-lattice summand of `e6Fourth` with the Bourbaki
simple-root model `typeE₆RootLattice` on `Fin 6 → ℚ`. -/
noncomputable def e6FourthComponentIsometry
    (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length) :
    IntegralLattice.Isometry
      ((RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rootLattice
        (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType i))
      typeE₆RootLattice :=
  ((RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rootLatticeIsometryOfEq
      (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType i)
      (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i) isSimplyLaced_E6).trans
    (IntegralLattice.Isometry.ofEq (rootLattice_E6 isSimplyLaced_E6))

/-- `e6FourthComponentIsometry` preserves every Bourbaki simple-root coordinate. -/
theorem e6FourthComponentIsometry_apply
    (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length)
    (v : Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ) (k : Fin 6) :
    e6FourthComponentIsometry i v k =
      v (Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
          (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)).trans rank_E6).symm k) := by
  rw [e6FourthComponentIsometry]
  -- `rootLattice_E6` identifies ambient spaces `Fin E6.rank → ℚ` and `Fin 6 → ℚ`, whose module
  -- instances match at semireducible transparency.
  exact (congrFun (IntegralLattice.Isometry.trans_apply _ _ v) k).trans <|
    (congrFun (IntegralLattice.Isometry.ofEq_apply (rootLattice_E6 isSimplyLaced_E6) _) k).trans <|
      DynkinType.rootLatticeIsometryOfEq_apply (s := .E6) _ _ _ _ v k

/-- The inverse of `e6FourthComponentIsometry` writes a `Fin 6 → ℚ` vector into the `i`-th table
component. -/
theorem e6FourthComponentIsometry_symm_apply
    (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length)
    (y : Fin 6 → ℚ) (k : Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank) :
    (e6FourthComponentIsometry i).symm y k =
      y (Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
          (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)).trans rank_E6) k) := by
  have hy : e6FourthComponentIsometry i
      (fun k' ↦ y (Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
          (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)).trans rank_E6) k')) = y := by
    ext k'
    rw [e6FourthComponentIsometry_apply, Fin.cast_cast, Fin.cast_eq_self]
  conv_lhs => rw [← hy, (e6FourthComponentIsometry i).symm_apply_apply]

private theorem glueModuleIsometry_apply_eq_ofEq
    (w : RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueModule)
    (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length) :
    FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.ofEq
        (glueAlphabet_congr (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)
          (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType i) isSimplyLaced_E6) (w i) =
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w
        (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i) := by
  have heq : DynkinType.piGlueAlphabetCongr RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType
      (finCongr RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth.symm)
      (fun k ↦ RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth _) w =
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w :=
    encodeGlueWord_injective _ _
      ((encodeGlueWord_piGlueAlphabetCongr _ _ _ _ _ w).trans
        (RootfulNiemeierType.encodeGlueWord_glueModuleIsometry _ _ _ _ w).symm)
  have happ := congrFun heq (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i)
  rw [DynkinType.piGlueAlphabetCongr_apply] at happ
  generalize hidx : (finCongr RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth.symm)
    (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i) = i' at happ
  have hi : i' = i := hidx.symm.trans (by simp)
  subst hi
  exact happ

private theorem discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthComponentIsometry_glueAlphabetIsometry
    (w : RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueModule)
    (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length) :
    (e6FourthComponentIsometry i).discriminantGroupEquiv
        ((RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).glueAlphabetIsometry
          (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType i)
          (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType i) (w i)) =
      typeE₆DiscriminantGroupEquiv
        ((RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3)
          (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i)) := by
  have h1 := (glueAlphabetIsometry_ofEq (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)
    (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType i) valid_E6
    (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType i) isSimplyLaced_E6 (w i)).symm
  -- `discriminantQuadraticIsometry` lands in the discriminant quadratic-module carrier, which
  -- `erw` identifies with the underlying discriminant group.
  erw [IntegralLattice.Isometry.discriminantQuadraticIsometry_apply] at h1
  rw [glueModuleIsometry_apply_eq_ofEq] at h1
  rw [e6FourthComponentIsometry]
  erw [IntegralLattice.Isometry.discriminantGroupEquiv_trans, LinearEquiv.trans_apply, h1,
    glueAlphabetIsometry_E6_apply,
    ← IntegralLattice.Isometry.symm_ofEq (rootLattice_E6 isSimplyLaced_E6),
    IntegralLattice.Isometry.discriminantGroupEquiv_symm, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- **The `E₆⁴` root-lattice comparison**: identifying each of the four `E₆` components with
`typeE₆RootLattice` and swapping the first two blocks gives an isometry onto
`typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower (Fin 4)`. -/
noncomputable def e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry :
    IntegralLattice.Isometry RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice
      (typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) :=
  (IntegralLattice.Isometry.pi e6FourthComponentIsometry).trans
    (IntegralLattice.Isometry.piCongrLeft (fun _ : Fin 4 ↦ typeE₆RootLattice)
      ((finCongr RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth).trans
        RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm))

/-- At block `j : Fin 4` and simple-root coordinate `k : Fin 6`, `e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry`
reads table component `e6FourthTetracodePerm j` at coordinate `k`. -/
theorem e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry_apply
    (x : ∀ i, Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ)
    (j : Fin 4) (k : Fin 6) :
    e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry x j k =
      x (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth.symm
          (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j))
        (Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
            (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth _)).trans rank_E6).symm k) := by
  let σ := (finCongr RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth).trans
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
  have h := IntegralLattice.Isometry.piCongrLeft_apply_apply
    (fun _ : Fin 4 ↦ typeE₆RootLattice) σ
    (IntegralLattice.Isometry.pi e6FourthComponentIsometry x) (σ.symm j)
  rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply] at h
  have hσ : σ.symm j = Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth.symm
      (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j) := by
    simp [σ]
  rw [e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry, IntegralLattice.Isometry.trans_apply,
    congrFun h k, IntegralLattice.Isometry.pi_apply, e6FourthComponentIsometry_apply]
  generalize hm : σ.symm j = m
  rw [hm] at hσ
  subst hσ
  rfl

/-- **The root-lattice comparison acts on glue words by `e6FourthTetracodeIsometry`**: it carries
the discriminant class of a glue word `w` of `e6Fourth` to the coordinate-power discriminant class
of the ternary word `e6FourthTetracodeIsometry w`. -/
theorem discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry_glueWordIsometry
    (w : RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueModule) :
    e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry.discriminantGroupEquiv
        (DynkinType.glueWordIsometry RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType
          RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType
          RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType w) =
      typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry.coordinatePowerDiscriminant (Fin 4)
        (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry w) := by
  apply (discriminantGroupPiEquiv fun _ : Fin 4 ↦ typeE₆RootLattice).injective
  funext j
  let σ := (finCongr RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth).trans
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
  have hperm := discriminantGroupPiEquiv_discriminantGroupEquiv_piCongrLeft
    (fun _ : Fin 4 ↦ typeE₆RootLattice) σ
    ((IntegralLattice.Isometry.pi e6FourthComponentIsometry).discriminantGroupEquiv
      (DynkinType.glueWordIsometry RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType
        RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType
        RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType w)) (σ.symm j)
  rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply] at hperm
  rw [e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry, IntegralLattice.Isometry.discriminantGroupEquiv_trans]
  -- `glueWordIsometry` and `coordinatePowerDiscriminant` land in discriminant quadratic-module
  -- carriers, which `erw` identifies with the underlying discriminant groups.
  erw [LinearEquiv.trans_apply, hperm, discriminantGroupPiEquiv_discriminantGroupEquiv_pi,
    discriminantGroupPiEquiv_glueWordIsometry,
    discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthComponentIsometry_glueAlphabetIsometry,
    FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.discriminantGroupPiEquiv_coordinatePowerDiscriminant_apply]
  have hidx : Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth (σ.symm j) =
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j := by
    simp [σ]
  rw [hidx, ← RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply]
  exact (typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry_apply _).symm

private theorem map_discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry :
    (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueSubgroup.map
        (DynkinType.glueWordIsometry RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType
          RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType
          RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType).toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom).map
      e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry.discriminantGroupEquiv.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom =
      codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant tetracode.toAddSubgroup := by
  have hcode : codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant tetracode.toAddSubgroup =
      tetracode.toAddSubgroup.map
        (typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry.coordinatePowerDiscriminant
          (Fin 4)).toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom :=
    AddSubgroup.ext fun x ↦ (mem_codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant_iff _ x).trans
      AddSubgroup.mem_map_equiv.symm
  refine Eq.trans ?_ hcode.symm
  exact (AddSubgroup.map_map _ _ _).trans <|
    ((congrArg RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueSubgroup.map
      (AddMonoidHom.ext
        discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry_glueWordIsometry)).trans
      (AddSubgroup.map_map _ _ _).symm).trans
    (congrArg (AddSubgroup.map _) RootfulNiemeierType.map_glueSubgroup_e6FourthTetracodeIsometry)

/-- **`niemeierE6Fourth` is the ternary tetracode gluing of `(E₆)⁴`**: an explicit isometry from
the table lattice `niemeierE6Fourth` onto the overlattice of `typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower
(Fin 4)` glued along `TauCeti.tetracode` via `TauCeti.codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant`. -/
noncomputable def niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry :
    IntegralLattice.Isometry niemeierE6Fourth
      ((typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower (Fin 4)).ofIsotropicSubgroup
        (isEven_typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower (Fin 4))
        (codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant tetracode.toAddSubgroup)
        Tetracode.isLagrangian_codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant.isIsotropic) :=
  (IntegralLattice.Isometry.ofEq
      ((RootfulNiemeierType.lattice_def .e6Fourth).trans (gluedLattice_def _ _ _ _ _))).trans
    (e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry.ofIsotropicSubgroups (isEven_pi_rootLattice _ _) _ _ _
      map_discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry)

/-- At tetracode coordinate `j : Fin 4` and Bourbaki simple-root coordinate `k : Fin 6`,
`niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry` reads table component `e6FourthTetracodePerm j` at coordinate
`k`. -/
@[simp]
theorem niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply
    (x : ∀ i, Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ)
    (j : Fin 4) (k : Fin 6) :
    niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry x j k =
      x (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth.symm
          (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j))
        (Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
            (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth _)).trans rank_E6).symm k) := by
  unfold niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry
  -- Isotropy proofs live on discriminant quadratic-module carriers, which `erw` identifies with
  -- the underlying discriminant groups.
  erw [IntegralLattice.Isometry.trans_apply, IntegralLattice.Isometry.ofEq_apply,
    IntegralLattice.Isometry.ofIsotropicSubgroups_apply]
  exact e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry_apply x j k

/-- The inverse of `niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry` places tetracode block
`e6FourthTetracodePerm i` into table component `i`. -/
-- Not `@[simp]`: `simp` rewrites `e6Fourth.componentType i` inside the argument `k` by
-- `componentType_e6Fourth`.
theorem niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry_symm_apply
    (y : Fin 4 → Fin 6 → ℚ)
    (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length)
    (k : Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank) :
    niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry.symm y i k =
      y (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
          (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i))
        (Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
            (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)).trans rank_E6) k) := by
  have hy : niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry (fun i' k' ↦
      y (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
          (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i'))
        (Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
            (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i')).trans rank_E6) k')) = y := by
    ext j k'
    rw [niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply]
    have hperm : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
        (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth
          (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth.symm
            (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j))) = j := by
      rw [Fin.cast_cast, Fin.cast_eq_self]
      nth_rw 1 [← RootfulNiemeierType.symm_e6FourthTetracodePerm]
      exact Equiv.symm_apply_apply _ _
    simp only [Fin.cast_cast, Fin.cast_eq_self]
    exact congrArg (fun m ↦ y m k') hperm
  conv_lhs => rw [← hy, niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry.symm_apply_apply]

/-- `niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry` carries the root sublattice of `e6Fourth` onto the
simple-root coordinate power `(E₆)⁴`. -/
theorem map_rootLattice_carrier_niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry :
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice.carrier.map
        niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry.ambientEquiv.toLinearMap =
      (typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower (Fin 4)).carrier := by
  have heq : niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry.ambientEquiv =
      e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry.ambientEquiv := by
    refine IntegralLattice.Isometry.ambientEquiv_eq_of_forall_apply_eq fun x ↦ ?_
    ext j k
    rw [niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply, e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry_apply]
  rw [heq, e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry.map_carrier_ambientEquiv]

/-! ### Explicit norm-`4` minuscule-weight generators and nine-coset carrier -/

/-- Integer coefficients `(0, 1, 1, 1)` and `(1, 0, 1, -1)` in `{-1, 0, 1}` realizing the two
`𝔽₃`-basis glue words `[0111]` and `[1012]` of `E₆⁴` via multiples of the minuscule weight
`ϖ₁ = typeE₆MinusculeWeight`. -/
@[expose] def e6FourthGlueCoeff : Fin 2 → Fin 4 → ℤ
  | 0 => ![0, 1, 1, 1]
  | 1 => ![1, 0, 1, -1]

/-- The zeroth `E₆⁴` glue-coefficient vector is `![0, 1, 1, 1]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem e6FourthGlueCoeff_zero : e6FourthGlueCoeff 0 = ![0, 1, 1, 1] := rfl

/-- The first `E₆⁴` glue-coefficient vector is `![1, 0, 1, -1]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem e6FourthGlueCoeff_one : e6FourthGlueCoeff 1 = ![1, 0, 1, -1] := rfl

/-- **Two explicit norm-`4` glue vectors generating `niemeierE6Fourth` over its root lattice**:
`e6FourthGlueVector 0` is `(0, ϖ₁, ϖ₁, ϖ₁)` (glue word `[0111]`) and `e6FourthGlueVector 1` is
`(ϖ₁, 0, ϖ₁, -ϖ₁)` (glue word `[1012]`), written in Bourbaki simple-root coordinates on each `E₆`
component. -/
noncomputable def e6FourthGlueVector (b : Fin 2) :
    ∀ i, Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ :=
  fun i ↦ e6FourthGlueCoeff b (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i) •
    (e6FourthComponentIsometry i).symm typeE₆MinusculeWeight

/-- Explicit coordinate formula for `e6FourthGlueVector`: component `i` at simple-root index `j` is
`e6FourthGlueCoeff b i` times the corresponding Bourbaki coordinate of `typeE₆MinusculeWeight`. -/
theorem e6FourthGlueVector_apply (b : Fin 2)
    (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length)
    (j : Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank) :
    e6FourthGlueVector b i j =
      (e6FourthGlueCoeff b (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i) : ℚ) *
        typeE₆MinusculeWeight
          (Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
              (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)).trans rank_E6) j) := by
  rw [e6FourthGlueVector, Pi.smul_apply, e6FourthComponentIsometry_symm_apply, zsmul_eq_mul]

/-- Both `e6FourthGlueVector 0` and `e6FourthGlueVector 1` lie in the dual of
`e6Fourth.rootLattice`. -/
theorem e6FourthGlueVector_mem_dualCarrier (b : Fin 2) :
    e6FourthGlueVector b ∈ RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice.dualCarrier := by
  rw [mem_dualCarrier_pi_iff]
  intro i
  rw [e6FourthGlueVector]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _
    (((e6FourthComponentIsometry i).symm.apply_mem_dualCarrier_iff _).mpr
      typeE₆MinusculeWeight_mem_dualCarrier)

private noncomputable def e6FourthBasisGlueWord (b : Fin 2) :
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueModule :=
  RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry.symm
    (fun k ↦ (e6FourthGlueCoeff b k : ZMod 3))

private theorem e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_e6FourthBasisGlueWord (b : Fin 2) :
    (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry (e6FourthBasisGlueWord b) : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) =
      tetracodeGenerator b := by
  let u : Fin 4 → ZMod 3 :=
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry (e6FourthBasisGlueWord b)
  let v : Fin 4 → ZMod 3 :=
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry (e6FourthBasisGlueWord b)
  have hu : u = fun k ↦ (e6FourthGlueCoeff b k : ZMod 3) :=
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry.apply_symm_apply _
  have hv (j : Fin 4) : v j = u (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j) :=
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply _ j
  have p0 : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm 0 = 1 := rfl
  have p1 : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm 1 = 0 := rfl
  have p2 : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm 2 = 2 := rfl
  have p3 : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm 3 = 3 := rfl
  have hveq : v = tetracodeGenerator b := by
    funext j
    rw [hv j, hu, tetracodeGenerator_def]
    fin_cases b <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [p0, p1, p2, p3]
  exact hveq

private theorem tetracodeGenerator_mem_tetracode (b : Fin 2) :
    tetracodeGenerator b ∈ tetracode := by
  rw [mem_tetracode_iff, tetracodeGenerator_def]
  fin_cases b <;> decide

private theorem closure_pair_e6FourthBasisGlueWord :
    AddSubgroup.closure {e6FourthBasisGlueWord 0, e6FourthBasisGlueWord 1} =
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueSubgroup := by
  apply AddSubgroup.map_injective
    (f := RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom)
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.toAddEquiv.injective
  have hrhs : RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueSubgroup.map
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom =
      tetracode.toAddSubgroup :=
    RootfulNiemeierType.map_glueSubgroup_e6FourthTetracodeIsometry
  rw [hrhs, AddMonoidHom.map_closure]
  refine le_antisymm ((AddSubgroup.closure_le _).mpr ?_) fun x hx ↦ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
    -- Membership in the coordinate-power carrier is membership in `tetracode`.
    change (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry w : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) ∈ tetracode
    rcases Set.mem_insert_iff.mp hw with rfl | hw
    · rw [e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_e6FourthBasisGlueWord]
      exact tetracodeGenerator_mem_tetracode 0
    · rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp hw, e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_e6FourthBasisGlueWord]
      exact tetracodeGenerator_mem_tetracode 1
  · set H := AddSubgroup.closure
      ((RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom :
          RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueModule →+
            typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) ''
        ({e6FourthBasisGlueWord 0, e6FourthBasisGlueWord 1} :
          Set RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueModule))
    have hrow (b : Fin 2) :
        (tetracodeGenerator b : typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) ∈ H := by
      have hmem : e6FourthBasisGlueWord b ∈
          ({e6FourthBasisGlueWord 0, e6FourthBasisGlueWord 1} :
            Set RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueModule) := by
        fin_cases b <;> simp
      have hin : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry (e6FourthBasisGlueWord b) ∈ H :=
        AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨e6FourthBasisGlueWord b, hmem, rfl⟩
      exact (e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_e6FourthBasisGlueWord b) ▸ hin
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := (tetracode_def ▸ Matrix.mem_generatedBy_iff).mp hx
    rw [Matrix.vecMul_eq_sum, Fin.sum_univ_two]
    have hsmul (b : Fin 2) :
        (a b • tetracodeGenerator b :
          typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower (Fin 4)) ∈ H := by
      rw [← ZMod.natCast_zmod_val (a b), Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul]
      exact H.nsmul_mem (hrow b) _
    exact H.add_mem (hsmul 0) (hsmul 1)

private theorem discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthComponentIsometry_e6FourthGlueVector
    (b : Fin 2) (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length) :
    (e6FourthComponentIsometry i).discriminantGroupEquiv
        (Submodule.Quotient.mk ((piDualCarrierEquiv _)
          ⟨e6FourthGlueVector b, e6FourthGlueVector_mem_dualCarrier b⟩ i)) =
      typeE₆DiscriminantGroupEquiv
        (e6FourthGlueCoeff b
          (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i) : ZMod 3) := by
  rw [IntegralLattice.Isometry.discriminantGroupEquiv_mk]
  have hval : (e6FourthComponentIsometry i).dualCarrierEquiv
      ((piDualCarrierEquiv _)
        ⟨e6FourthGlueVector b, e6FourthGlueVector_mem_dualCarrier b⟩ i) =
      e6FourthGlueCoeff b
          (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i) •
        typeE₆MinusculeWeightDual := by
    ext k
    simp only [IntegralLattice.Isometry.coe_dualCarrierEquiv_apply, coe_piDualCarrierEquiv_apply,
      e6FourthGlueVector, map_zsmul, IntegralLattice.Isometry.apply_symm_apply,
      SetLike.val_smul, coe_typeE₆MinusculeWeightDual]
  rw [hval, Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, mk_typeE₆MinusculeWeightDual,
    ← typeE₆DiscriminantGroupEquiv_apply_one, ← map_zsmul, zsmul_one]

private theorem mk_e6FourthGlueVector (b : Fin 2) :
    (Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨e6FourthGlueVector b, e6FourthGlueVector_mem_dualCarrier b⟩ :
        RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice.DiscriminantGroup) =
      DynkinType.glueWordIsometry RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType
        RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType
        RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType (e6FourthBasisGlueWord b) := by
  apply e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry.discriminantGroupEquiv.injective
  rw [discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry_glueWordIsometry]
  apply (discriminantGroupPiEquiv fun _ : Fin 4 ↦ typeE₆RootLattice).injective
  funext j
  let σ := (finCongr RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth).trans
    RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
  have hperm := discriminantGroupPiEquiv_discriminantGroupEquiv_piCongrLeft
    (fun _ : Fin 4 ↦ typeE₆RootLattice) σ
    ((IntegralLattice.Isometry.pi e6FourthComponentIsometry).discriminantGroupEquiv
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨e6FourthGlueVector b, e6FourthGlueVector_mem_dualCarrier b⟩))
    (σ.symm j)
  rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply] at hperm
  rw [e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry, IntegralLattice.Isometry.discriminantGroupEquiv_trans,
    LinearEquiv.trans_apply, hperm, discriminantGroupPiEquiv_discriminantGroupEquiv_pi,
    discriminantGroupPiEquiv_mk]
  -- `coordinatePowerDiscriminant` acts on the quadratic-module carrier underlying the discriminant
  -- group.
  erw [FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.discriminantGroupPiEquiv_coordinatePowerDiscriminant_apply,
    typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry_apply]
  have hword : (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry (e6FourthBasisGlueWord b) :
      Fin 4 → ZMod 3) j =
      (e6FourthGlueCoeff b (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ZMod 3) := by
    rw [RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply]
    exact congrFun (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthGlueModuleIsometry.apply_symm_apply _) _
  rw [discriminantGroupEquiv_e6FourthComponentIsometry_e6FourthGlueVector]
  refine (congrArg (fun m ↦ typeE₆DiscriminantGroupEquiv (e6FourthGlueCoeff b m : ZMod 3)) ?_).trans
    (congrArg typeE₆DiscriminantGroupEquiv hword.symm)
  simp [σ]

/-- **Both explicit minuscule-weight glue vectors belong to `niemeierE6Fourth`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem e6FourthGlueVector_mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier (b : Fin 2) :
    e6FourthGlueVector b ∈ niemeierE6Fourth.carrier := by
  rw [mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_iff_tetracode]
  refine ⟨e6FourthGlueVector_mem_dualCarrier b, ?_⟩
  rw [mk_e6FourthGlueVector]
  have hsymm : (DynkinType.glueWordIsometry RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType).toAddEquiv.symm
      (DynkinType.glueWordIsometry RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType
        RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.isSimplyLaced_componentType
        RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.valid_componentType (e6FourthBasisGlueWord b)) =
      e6FourthBasisGlueWord b :=
    AddEquiv.symm_apply_apply _ _
  rw [hsymm, e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_e6FourthBasisGlueWord]
  exact tetracodeGenerator_mem_tetracode b

/-- **Both explicit minuscule-weight glue vectors have squared norm `4`.** -/
-- Not `@[simp]`: `simp` rewrites `niemeierE6Fourth.form` via `RootfulNiemeierType.lattice_form`.
theorem form_e6FourthGlueVector_self (b : Fin 2) :
    niemeierE6Fourth.form (e6FourthGlueVector b) (e6FourthGlueVector b) = 4 := by
  rw [RootfulNiemeierType.lattice_form,
    ← e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry.map_app (e6FourthGlueVector b) (e6FourthGlueVector b),
    pi_form, piForm_apply]
  have hcoord (j : Fin 4) : e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry (e6FourthGlueVector b) j =
      (e6FourthGlueCoeff b (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ℚ) •
        typeE₆MinusculeWeight := by
    ext k
    rw [e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry_apply, e6FourthGlueVector_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul,
      Fin.cast_cast, Fin.cast_eq_self, Fin.cast_cast, Fin.cast_eq_self]
  have hpair (j : Fin 4) :
      typeE₆RootLattice.form (e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry (e6FourthGlueVector b) j)
        (e6FourthTetracodeRootIsometry (e6FourthGlueVector b) j) =
        (e6FourthGlueCoeff b (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm j) : ℚ) ^ 2 *
          (4 / 3) := by
    rw [hcoord j, map_smul, map_smul, LinearMap.smul_apply, form_typeE₆MinusculeWeight_self,
      smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
    ring
  have p0 : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm 0 = 1 := rfl
  have p1 : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm 1 = 0 := rfl
  have p2 : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm 2 = 2 := rfl
  have p3 : RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm 3 = 3 := rfl
  simp only [hpair, Fin.sum_univ_four, p0, p1, p2, p3]
  fin_cases b <;> norm_num [e6FourthGlueCoeff]

/-- **The root lattice and the two explicit norm-`4` minuscule-weight glue vectors generate
`niemeierE6Fourth` over `ℤ`.** -/
theorem niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_eq_sup_span :
    niemeierE6Fourth.carrier =
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice.carrier ⊔
        Submodule.span ℤ {e6FourthGlueVector 0, e6FourthGlueVector 1} := by
  have hne : e6FourthBasisGlueWord 1 ≠ e6FourthBasisGlueWord 0 := by
    intro h
    have ht : (tetracodeGenerator 1 : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) 0 =
        (tetracodeGenerator 0 : Fin 4 → ZMod 3) 0 := by
      rw [← e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_e6FourthBasisGlueWord 1,
        ← e6FourthTetracodeIsometry_e6FourthBasisGlueWord 0, h]
    simp [tetracodeGenerator_def] at ht
  classical
  let rep : RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.glueModule →
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice.dualCarrier :=
    fun w ↦ if w = e6FourthBasisGlueWord 0 then
      ⟨e6FourthGlueVector 0, e6FourthGlueVector_mem_dualCarrier 0⟩
    else
      ⟨e6FourthGlueVector 1, e6FourthGlueVector_mem_dualCarrier 1⟩
  rw [niemeierE6Fourth, RootfulNiemeierType.lattice_def,
    DynkinType.gluedLattice_carrier_eq_sup_span _ _ _ _ _ closure_pair_e6FourthBasisGlueWord rep]
  · congr 2
    rw [Set.image_pair]
    simp [rep, hne]
  · intro w hw
    rcases Set.mem_insert_iff.mp hw with rfl | hw
    · simp only [rep, ↓reduceIte]
      exact mk_e6FourthGlueVector 0
    · rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hw
      subst hw
      simp only [rep, hne, ↓reduceIte]
      exact mk_e6FourthGlueVector 1

/-- Three times each basis glue vector lies in the root lattice `e6Fourth.rootLattice`. -/
theorem three_nsmul_e6FourthGlueVector_mem_rootLattice_carrier (b : Fin 2) :
    3 • e6FourthGlueVector b ∈ RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice.carrier := by
  rw [IntegralLattice.mem_pi_carrier_iff]
  intro i
  rw [DynkinType.mem_rootLattice_carrier_iff]
  intro j
  let k : Fin 6 :=
    Fin.cast ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
      (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)).trans rank_E6) j
  refine ⟨e6FourthGlueCoeff b (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i) *
      (![4, 3, 5, 6, 4, 2] : Fin 6 → ℤ) k, ?_⟩
  rw [Pi.smul_apply, Pi.smul_apply, e6FourthGlueVector_apply, typeE₆MinusculeWeight_apply,
    nsmul_eq_mul]
  push_cast
  ring

/-- **Explicit nine-coset decomposition of `niemeierE6Fourth`**: a vector belongs to the table
lattice if and only if subtracting a combination `a₀ • g₀ + a₁ • g₁` with `a₀, a₁ ∈ {0, 1, 2}`
lands in the root lattice `e6Fourth.rootLattice`. -/
theorem mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_iff_exists_fin_three
    (x : ∀ i, Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ) :
    x ∈ niemeierE6Fourth.carrier ↔
      ∃ a₀ a₁ : Fin 3,
        x - (a₀ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 0 - (a₁ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 1 ∈
          RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice.carrier := by
  constructor
  · intro hx
    rw [niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_eq_sup_span, Submodule.mem_sup] at hx
    obtain ⟨r, hr, y, hy, rfl⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨c₀, c₁, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_pair.mp hy
    let a₀ : Fin 3 := ⟨(c₀ % 3).toNat, by omega⟩
    let a₁ : Fin 3 := ⟨(c₁ % 3).toNat, by omega⟩
    refine ⟨a₀, a₁, ?_⟩
    have hc (c : ℤ) (b : Fin 2) :
        c • e6FourthGlueVector b - ((c % 3).toNat : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector b =
          (c / 3) • (3 • e6FourthGlueVector b) := by
      have hdiv : c = (c / 3) * 3 + ((c % 3).toNat : ℤ) := by omega
      calc c • e6FourthGlueVector b - ((c % 3).toNat : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector b
          = ((c / 3) * 3 + ((c % 3).toNat : ℤ)) • e6FourthGlueVector b -
              ((c % 3).toNat : ℤ) • e6FourthGlueVector b := by
            rw [← hdiv, Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul]
        _ = ((c / 3) * 3) • e6FourthGlueVector b := by
            rw [add_zsmul, add_sub_cancel_right]
        _ = (c / 3) • (3 • e6FourthGlueVector b) := mul_zsmul _ _ _
    have hrew : r + (c₀ • e6FourthGlueVector 0 + c₁ • e6FourthGlueVector 1) -
          (a₀ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 0 - (a₁ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 1 =
        r + (c₀ / 3) • (3 • e6FourthGlueVector 0) +
          (c₁ / 3) • (3 • e6FourthGlueVector 1) := by
      rw [← hc c₀ 0, ← hc c₁ 1]
      abel
    rw [hrew]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _
      (Submodule.add_mem _ hr
        (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (three_nsmul_e6FourthGlueVector_mem_rootLattice_carrier 0)))
      (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (three_nsmul_e6FourthGlueVector_mem_rootLattice_carrier 1))
  · rintro ⟨a₀, a₁, hmem⟩
    have hr : x - (a₀ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 0 - (a₁ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 1 ∈
        niemeierE6Fourth.carrier :=
      RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.rootLattice_carrier_le_lattice_carrier hmem
    have hadd := Submodule.add_mem _
      (Submodule.add_mem _ hr
        (nsmul_mem (e6FourthGlueVector_mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier 0) a₀))
      (nsmul_mem (e6FourthGlueVector_mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier 1) a₁)
    have hcancel : x - (a₀ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 0 - (a₁ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 1 +
        (a₀ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 0 + (a₁ : ℕ) • e6FourthGlueVector 1 = x := by
      abel
    rwa [hcancel] at hadd

/-- **Literal carrier of `niemeierE6Fourth` in Bourbaki simple-root coordinates**: a family `x` of
four rational vectors lies in `niemeierE6Fourth` if and only if for some `a₀, a₁ ∈ {0, 1, 2}`, all
twenty-four simple-root coordinates of `x - a₀ • e6FourthGlueVector 0 - a₁ • e6FourthGlueVector 1`
are integers. -/
theorem mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_iff_int_coords
    (x : ∀ i, Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ) :
    x ∈ niemeierE6Fourth.carrier ↔
      ∃ a₀ a₁ : Fin 3, ∀ i j, ∃ z : ℤ,
        (z : ℚ) = x i j - (a₀ : ℕ) * e6FourthGlueVector 0 i j -
          (a₁ : ℕ) * e6FourthGlueVector 1 i j := by
  rw [mem_niemeierE6Fourth_carrier_iff_exists_fin_three]
  refine exists_congr fun a₀ ↦ exists_congr fun a₁ ↦ ?_
  rw [IntegralLattice.mem_pi_carrier_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun i ↦ (DynkinType.mem_rootLattice_carrier_iff _ _ _).trans ?_
  exact forall_congr' fun j ↦ exists_congr fun z ↦ by
    simp only [Pi.sub_apply, Pi.smul_apply]
    simp only [nsmul_eq_mul]

/-! ### Monomial automorphisms of ternary codes and of the tetracode -/

section MonomialAut

variable {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]

/-- Signed coordinate permutation of the orthogonal power `typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower ι`,
scaling block `i` by `v i` and moving it to block `e i`. -/
noncomputable def typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry (v : ι → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm ι) :
    IntegralLattice.Isometry (typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower ι)
      (typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower ι) :=
  (IntegralLattice.Isometry.pi fun i ↦
      IntegralLattice.Isometry.unitsSMul (v i) typeE₆RootLattice).trans
    (IntegralLattice.Isometry.piCongrLeft (fun _ : ι ↦ typeE₆RootLattice) e)

/-- At coordinate `j : ι`, `typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry` scales coordinate `e.symm j` by
`v (e.symm j)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry_apply (v : ι → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm ι)
    (y : ι → Fin 6 → ℚ) (j : ι) :
    typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry v e y j = (v (e.symm j) : ℤ) • y (e.symm j) := by
  obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := e.surjective j
  rw [typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry, IntegralLattice.Isometry.trans_apply,
    IntegralLattice.Isometry.piCongrLeft_apply_apply, IntegralLattice.Isometry.pi_apply,
    Equiv.symm_apply_apply, IntegralLattice.Isometry.unitsSMul_apply]

/-- `typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry v e` acts on ternary `E₆` discriminant words by
`signedEquiv v e`. -/
theorem discriminantGroupEquiv_typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry
    (v : ι → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm ι) (w : ι → ZMod 3) :
    (typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry v e).discriminantGroupEquiv
        (typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry.coordinatePowerDiscriminant ι w) =
      typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry.coordinatePowerDiscriminant ι
        (signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) v e w) := by
  apply (discriminantGroupPiEquiv fun _ : ι ↦ typeE₆RootLattice).injective
  funext j
  obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := e.surjective j
  rw [typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry, IntegralLattice.Isometry.discriminantGroupEquiv_trans]
  -- `coordinatePowerDiscriminant` acts on the quadratic-module carrier, which `erw` identifies
  -- with `ι → ZMod 3` and the underlying discriminant group.
  erw [LinearEquiv.trans_apply, discriminantGroupPiEquiv_discriminantGroupEquiv_piCongrLeft,
    discriminantGroupPiEquiv_discriminantGroupEquiv_pi,
    IntegralLattice.Isometry.discriminantGroupEquiv_unitsSMul_apply,
    FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.discriminantGroupPiEquiv_coordinatePowerDiscriminant_apply,
    FiniteQuadraticModule.Isometry.discriminantGroupPiEquiv_coordinatePowerDiscriminant_apply,
    typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry_apply, typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry_apply]
  rw [← map_zsmul, signedEquiv_apply, Equiv.symm_apply_apply, zsmul_eq_mul]

private theorem map_codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant_signedIsometry
    (C : LinearCode (ZMod 3) ι) (v : ι → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm ι)
    (he : signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) v e ∈ monomialAut C) :
    (codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant C.toAddSubgroup).map
        (typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry v e).discriminantGroupEquiv.toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom =
      codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant C.toAddSubgroup := by
  have hcode : codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant C.toAddSubgroup =
      C.toAddSubgroup.map
        (typeE₆DiscriminantQuadraticIsometry.coordinatePowerDiscriminant
          ι).toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom :=
    AddSubgroup.ext fun x ↦ (mem_codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant_iff _ x).trans
      AddSubgroup.mem_map_equiv.symm
  have hmapC : C.toAddSubgroup.map (signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) v e).toAddEquiv.toAddMonoidHom =
      C.toAddSubgroup :=
    congrArg Submodule.toAddSubgroup (mem_monomialAut.mp he).2
  rw [hcode]
  exact (AddSubgroup.map_map _ _ _).trans <|
    ((congrArg C.toAddSubgroup.map
      (AddMonoidHom.ext (discriminantGroupEquiv_typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry v e))).trans
      (AddSubgroup.map_map _ _ _).symm).trans
    (congrArg (AddSubgroup.map _) hmapC)

/-- **Every monomial automorphism of a quadratic-isotropic ternary code `C` induces a self-isometry
of the corresponding `(E₆)^ι` overlattice.** -/
noncomputable def typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry (C : LinearCode (ZMod 3) ι)
    (hC : (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower ι).IsIsotropic C.toAddSubgroup)
    (v : ι → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm ι) (he : signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) v e ∈ monomialAut C) :
    IntegralLattice.Isometry
      ((typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower ι).ofIsotropicSubgroup
        (isEven_typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower ι)
        (codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant C.toAddSubgroup)
        ((isIsotropic_codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant_iff C.toAddSubgroup).mpr hC))
      ((typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower ι).ofIsotropicSubgroup
        (isEven_typeE₆RootLattice.coordinatePower ι)
        (codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant C.toAddSubgroup)
        ((isIsotropic_codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant_iff C.toAddSubgroup).mpr hC)) :=
  (typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry v e).ofIsotropicSubgroups _ _ _ _
    (map_codeInTypeE6CoordinatePowerDiscriminant_signedIsometry C v e he)

/-- `typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry` scales coordinate `e.symm j` by `v (e.symm j)` and moves it to
coordinate `j`. -/
@[simp]
theorem typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry_apply (C : LinearCode (ZMod 3) ι)
    (hC : (typeE₆StandardQuadraticModule.coordinatePower ι).IsIsotropic C.toAddSubgroup)
    (v : ι → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm ι) (he : signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) v e ∈ monomialAut C)
    (y : ι → Fin 6 → ℚ) (j : ι) :
    typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry C hC v e he y j = (v (e.symm j) : ℤ) • y (e.symm j) := by
  unfold typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry
  -- Isotropy proofs live on discriminant quadratic-module carriers underlying the discriminant
  -- group.
  erw [IntegralLattice.Isometry.ofIsotropicSubgroups_apply]
  exact typeE6CoordinatePowerSignedIsometry_apply v e y j

end MonomialAut

/-- **Every monomial automorphism of `TauCeti.tetracode` induces a self-isometry of the table
lattice `niemeierE6Fourth`**, obtained by conjugating `typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry` across
`niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry`. -/
noncomputable def niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry
    (v : Fin 4 → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm (Fin 4))
    (he : signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) v e ∈ monomialAut tetracode) :
    IntegralLattice.Isometry niemeierE6Fourth niemeierE6Fourth :=
  niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry.symm.conjMulEquiv
    (typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry tetracode Tetracode.isIsotropic_typeE6 v e he)

/-- `niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry` intertwines `niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry` with
`typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry` on the tetracode gluing of `(E₆)⁴`. -/
@[simp]
theorem niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry_niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry_apply
    (v : Fin 4 → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm (Fin 4))
    (he : signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) v e ∈ monomialAut tetracode)
    (x : ∀ i, Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank → ℚ) :
    niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry (niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry v e he x) =
      typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry tetracode Tetracode.isIsotropic_typeE6 v e he
        (niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry x) := by
  rw [niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry, IntegralLattice.Isometry.conjMulEquiv_apply,
    IntegralLattice.Isometry.symm_symm, IntegralLattice.Isometry.apply_symm_apply]

/-- Explicit coordinate formula for `niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry` on `niemeierE6Fourth`:
writing `p = e6FourthTetracodePerm`, table component `i` receives table component
`p (e.symm (p i))` scaled by the sign `v (e.symm (p i))`. -/
-- Not `@[simp]`: `simp` rewrites `e6Fourth.componentType i` inside the argument `k` by
-- `componentType_e6Fourth`.
theorem niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry_apply
    (v : Fin 4 → ℤˣ) (e : Equiv.Perm (Fin 4))
    (he : signedEquiv (R := ZMod 3) v e ∈ monomialAut tetracode)
    (x : ∀ m, Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType m).rank → ℚ)
    (i : Fin RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.components.length)
    (k : Fin (RootfulNiemeierType.e6Fourth.componentType i).rank) :
    niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry v e he x i k =
      (v (e.symm (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
          (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i))) : ℤ) •
        x (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth.symm
            (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
              (e.symm (RootfulNiemeierType.e6FourthTetracodePerm
                (Fin.cast RootfulNiemeierType.length_components_e6Fourth i)))))
          (Fin.cast (((congrArg DynkinType.rank
                (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth i)).trans rank_E6).trans
              ((congrArg DynkinType.rank
                (RootfulNiemeierType.componentType_e6Fourth _)).trans rank_E6).symm) k) := by
  rw [niemeierE6FourthTetracodeAutIsometry, IntegralLattice.Isometry.conjMulEquiv_apply,
    IntegralLattice.Isometry.symm_symm, niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry_symm_apply,
    typeE6CodeMonomialAutIsometry_apply, Pi.smul_apply, niemeierE6FourthTetracodeIsometry_apply,
    Fin.cast_cast]

end TauCeti
